 "notes": "Curve from Fig. 2 (figs/lim_photon_all.pdf in e-print): 90% CL NuSTAR quiescent-Sun limits on g_agamma with g_aee=0 (photon coupling responsible for both Primakoff production and a->2gamma decay), i.e. the paper's model-independent axion-photon result. Extracted the vector paths of all three method curves (Poisson, Yellin, CLs) and report the lower envelope of the union excluded region: below m~7 keV (CLs cutoff from the 4 keV photon-energy threshold) the boundary is the Yellin/Poisson curve; above, the CLs curve, which the paper states is the most stringent. Axis calibration verified via tick labels and the 1e-9 GeV^-1 clipping bound. Masses converted keV->eV. Not a dark-matter search (solar basin decay flux), so no rho_DM rescaling. The paper's Fig. 1 'universal coupling' limit on f (g_agamma=alpha/2pi f, g_aee=me/f) is stronger but model-dependent; not used.",
